From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Agent <hermes-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2026 10:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ci: apply migrations 0050 and 0051 in the CI chain

The CI steps that apply the association review ledger (0050) and the
family classification (0051).

THIS COMMIT NEEDS A HUMAN. The GitHub App has no 'workflows' scope and
cannot push it. Apply it with:

    git apply docs/ci-migrations-0050-0051.patch

Ordering: 0050 runs after the atlas fixtures, because the pilot samples
the association table the fixtures create. 0051 runs after 0050. Both
run after the seed.

REGENERATED 2026-11-07. The previous version of this patch was wrong in
two ways, and neither was visible until it was applied to main:

  1. It targeted `gustale` -- the LIVE database name. Every other
     migration step in this workflow targets `gustale_ci`, the CI
     service database. This was exactly the class of mistake the
     database-safety work removed from CI: a migration step that
     silently points at production. The steps now target `gustale_ci`.

  2. Its hunk header did not match main, so `git apply` failed
     outright. It had been generated against an older ci.yml.

The patch is now generated from main's actual .github/workflows/ci.yml
and verified with `git apply --check` against a pristine copy of it.

VERIFIED:
  * `git apply --check` against pristine main's ci.yml: clean.
  * Every `-d` target in the patched file is `gustale_ci` (35 of them);
    the live name appears zero times.

---
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 560104d..d0c7107 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -978,6 +978,34 @@ jobs:
           PGPASSWORD=gustale psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres -d gustale_ci -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 \
             -f packages/db/seed-atlas-fixtures.sql
 
+      # ── 0050: the association review ledger (Option C) ──────────────
+      #
+      # Creates `association_review_log` (the ledger), `association_sources`
+      # (the association <-> source link), the entity-integrity trigger,
+      # and the 50-row pilot.
+      #
+      # It writes NO published rows and re-points nothing.
+      #
+      # It must run AFTER the atlas fixtures: the pilot samples the
+      # association table, and the fixtures are what create the
+      # association rows it samples.
+      - name: Apply the association review ledger
+        run: |
+          PGPASSWORD=gustale psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres -d gustale_ci -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 \
+            -f db/migrations/0050_association_review_ledger.sql
+
+      # ── 0051: the family classification ─────────────────────────────
+      #
+      # Adds `dish_families.family_class` and applies the approved
+      # classification of all 306 families.
+      #
+      # It runs AFTER the atlas fixtures: its assertions count the
+      # families that carry a published dish.
+      - name: Apply the family classification
+        run: |
+          PGPASSWORD=gustale psql -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres -d gustale_ci -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 \
+            -f db/migrations/0051_family_classification.sql
+
       # The PER-DISH backfill assertions. LAST, because they assert the
       # state the whole chain produces: the reference dishes'
       # association rows AND the journey places in the editorial queue.

